# CODEOWNERS for a downstream KB repository (GitHub: .github/CODEOWNERS; GitLab: CODEOWNERS
# or .gitlab/CODEOWNERS). Replace the placeholders with real handles of your organization,
# for example `@your-org/kb-engine`; kb ships no default owners.
#   {{engine_owners}}     reviewers of engine updates (paths that come from upstream)
#   {{knowledge_owners}}  reviewers of project knowledge and its CI
# Code owners only request reviews. Making their approval mandatory requires branch
# protection / approval rules configured by an administrator.

# Engine-owned paths (core/release.toml `engine_paths`): change them through `kbw update`.
/kbw                      {{engine_owners}}
/Cargo.toml               {{engine_owners}}
/Cargo.lock               {{engine_owners}}
/rust-toolchain.toml      {{engine_owners}}
/core/                    {{engine_owners}}
/docs/                    {{engine_owners}}

# Project knowledge. Narrow it per group or repository when teams own different parts, e.g.
# /project/knowledge/repos/mobile/  @your-org/mobile
/project/                 {{knowledge_owners}}
/project/upstream.toml    {{engine_owners}}
/.github/workflows/kb-knowledge.yml {{knowledge_owners}}
